   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 Perfect Loop - Mobius route (experimental, t2va only)\n\nFollowing Mobius (arXiv:2502.20307): the **H3 Mobius Loop Patch** rotates the AV latent along time by a different offset at every denoising step and rotates the prediction back, so the wrap point is somewhere else each step and every frame is denoised with context from across the seam. The clip comes out cyclic by construction - no anchors, no post-hoc closure.\n\nRules of the route:\n- **Text-to-AV only.** No first/last frame, no references (the patch refuses them). For image-anchored loops use the Bridge workflow.\n- **Length**: use 56 / 107 / 158 / 209 / 260 / 311 - every third point of H3's 17g+5 grid, where the audio cycle closes exactly. 158 (~6.6s) is the default.\n- **H3 Mobius Loop Trim** cuts the first 5 frames afterwards: a clip's 2 leading latent steps sit outside the rotating cycle (they also absorb the VAE's cold start, so the wrap lands on a warm-decoded frame).\n- `shift_frames` 68 gives 9 distinct seam positions on a 158-frame clip. If a render still hitches at the wrap, try 51 or 85, more steps, or fall back to `wrap_crossfade_frames` 4-8 on the trim.\n\nThe seam-check Save plays the loop rolled by half so the wrap is mid-clip, visible in any player."
   ],
   "title": "README"
  },
